  "verbalization": "The compound in question, (4S,4aR,7aS,7bR)-4-hydroxy-6,6,7b-trimethyl-3-[[(2R,3R,4S,5S,6R)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxan-2-yl]oxymethyl]-1,2,4,4a,5,7a-hexahydrocyclobuta[g]inden-7-one, is shown to interact with WI-38, a cell line that is a target of both Dorsmannin A and Psoralidin. These two compounds are both known to interact with Leukocyte antigen CD37, suggesting a potential mechanism of action involving this receptor. The evidence indicates that the compound may act as a modulator of CD37 through its interaction with WI-38, which is a key target in the pathways involving CD37. The scores from the evidence suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, but further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the direct interaction and the specific mechanism of CD37 modulation.",
